        <briefdescription>
<para>Computes and propagates gradients for the tensor-scalar subtraction operation. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Implements the backward pass for tensor-scalar subtraction by passing the incoming gradient unchanged to the parent tensor. Since the derivative of subtraction with respect to the tensor input is unity and the scalar is treated as a constant, the gradient is propagated without modification. The method calls <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1function_1_1GradSubtractScalar_1a12c3c4e9ace4fce572a5af5cc3131252" kindref="member">backward()</ref> on the parent tensor&apos;s <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1GradFunction" kindref="compound">GradFunction</ref> to continue the backpropagation process.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>inputGradient</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The gradient of the loss with respect to the output of the subtraction operation </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>higherDerivative</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>If true, enables construction of a computational graph during the backward pass for higher-order derivatives; if false, disables gradient tracking </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
