    <briefdescription>
<para>Gradient function for tensor-scalar subtraction. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1function_1_1GradSubtractScalar" kindref="compound">GradSubtractScalar</ref> class represents the subtraction of a scalar value from a tensor in the computational graph, computing gradients for operations of the form <formula id="80">$C = A - s$</formula> where <formula id="12">$A$</formula> is a tensor and <formula id="13">$s$</formula> is a scalar value. The gradient computation follows from the derivative:   <formula id="14">\[    \frac{\partial C}{\partial A} = 1
\]</formula></para>
<para>The scalar value does not participate in gradient computation as it is a constant, not a learnable parameter or tensor that requires gradients. During backpropagation, the incoming gradient  <formula id="15">$\frac{\partial
L}{\partial C}$</formula> is passed unchanged to the parent tensor according to the chain rule:    <formula id="9">\[    \frac{\partial L}{\partial A} = \frac{\partial L}{\partial C} \cdot
\frac{\partial C}{\partial A} = \frac{\partial L}{\partial C}
\]</formula></para>
<para>This <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1GradFunction" kindref="compound">GradFunction</ref> saves the scalar value from the forward pass, though it is not strictly required for the gradient computation. The scalar is stored for potential use in higher-order derivative computations or for consistency with the gradient function interface.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1GradFunction" kindref="compound">GradFunction</ref> for the base class from which this class derives. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1function_1_1GradSubtract" kindref="compound">GradSubtract</ref> for the gradient function for elementwise tensor subtraction. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
